ethan: Heads-up — intermittent JSON parse errors in the Node SDK when using SSE streams. Happens when client disconnects mid-stream or when auth refresh occurs mid-stream. Repro in sample-app with node 18 + sdk 0.6.3. Anyone else seen this?

maya: saw something similar in python but handled differently. Node implementation parses per-event and chokes when an event is split across chunks.

vikas: can you paste a tiny repro + logs? /cc @tori for runtime side.

ethan: minimal client code: ```js
const req = http.request(url, { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${TOKEN}` } });
req.on('data', (chunk) => {
  // chunk could be partial: 'data: {"id":1, "text":"hel'
  // next chunk: 'lo"}'
  const lines = chunk.toString().split('\n\n');
  lines.forEach(line => {
    if (line.startsWith('data: ')) {
      const payload = JSON.parse(line.slice(6)); // throws on split
    }
  });
});
```
logs: `Error: Unexpected end of JSON input at JSON.parse (index.js:42)`
server logs show a token refresh around the same time: `auth: token refresh - 401 -> refresh success, reconnecting stream`

tori: that matches something we saw — runtime currently tears down the connection on auth rotate and opens a fresh one. If the SDK isn't preserving an incomplete event buffer the next connection loses the half-event -> parse error. Two approaches: server emits a control event with seq id so client replays/resumes, or client keeps a small trailing buffer across reconnects.

maya: +1 for seq id on events (e.g., `data: {"seq": 123, "payload": {...}}`). Clients can reassemble or detect gaps. Python SDK mostly works because we accidentally buffered across reconnects. Node doesn't.

vikas: SDK parity note: node lacks the resume buffer. I'll file a bug and patch node SDK to accumulate trailing partial chunk until full `\n\n` boundary before JSON.parse. Also add unit tests simulating connection abort mid-event.

ci-bot: Created issue #4387: "node sdk: sse parse errors on client abort/auth refresh - add resume/seq handling" assigned to vikas.

tori: interim workaround for sample apps: coalesce data events into a persistent buffer and only JSON.parse when you see `\n\n`. Also avoid rotating tokens during long streams (increase token TTL or use refresh ahead-of-time). Example: ```js
let buffer = '';
req.on('data', chunk => { buffer += chunk.toString(); let idx; while ((idx = buffer.indexOf('\n\n')) >= 0) { const raw = buffer.slice(0, idx); buffer = buffer.slice(idx + 2); if (raw.startsWith('data: ')) { try { const obj = JSON.parse(raw.slice(6)); /* handle */ } catch (e) { /* log and requeue */ } } } });
```

ethan: nice. I'll update our sample-app and onboarding guide to call out this edge case and recommended pattern. Also will add a short note: prefer sequence numbers from server for robust reassembly.

vikas: I'll push a short patch to node SDK today and add a telemetry metric for `sse_parse_error` so we can alert if it spikes.

ci-bot: Issue #4387 updated: labels: ["devex", "sdk-node", "priority-high"].

tori: runtime action item: avoid emitting 401 mid-stream where possible; if we must rotate, emit a `event: control\ndata: {"type":"resume_point","last_seq": 123}\n\n` so clients can reconcile. I'll open a runtime PR.

ethan: thanks all — assigning follow-ups: vikas (node SDK patch + tests), tori (runtime PR), me (sample-app + docs). Will check back after PRs merge. :thumbsup:
